			(table_cell "High-speed differential pairs carrying PCIe Gen1-6 data. PERLx+/– are the “Transmit” (Tx) lanes from the card; PERRx+/– (often on the opposite side) are the “Receive” (Rx) lanes back to the host. Signaling uses 8 b/10 b (Gen1-2) or 128 b/130 b (Gen3+) encoding."
